Subject: [PATCH] composite: finish source teardown before reopening its slot

A devnode removal does not itself close a running source or release EVIOGRAB.
Stop and join the owning task before clearing its state. Ignore queued task
completions from an earlier incarnation of the same eventN/hidrawN. Bound
teardown to five seconds and keep the slot occupied on timeout.

Regression coverage includes a task-incarnation unit test and Korri's real
USB HID gadget/udev/DBus/inputd capture VM, including node replay and bounce.

